          },
          {
            "topic": "Policy framework",
            "details": "Detail regulation and planning mechanisms, reforms, and stated or implicit goals (e.g., PDP8, REMA). Include key policy documents, their publication dates, and their implications for thermal power. Cite specific clauses or decisions where relevant."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Energy supply landscape",
            "details": "Analyze resources and reserves (domestic coal, gas, LNG), import dependencies, infrastructure (terminals, pipelines, interconnectors), and logistical constraints. Include maps or diagrams if available in sources."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Key institutional actors",
            "details": "List and describe the roles, influence, and relationships of Generation-Transmission-Distribution companies, Energy and Mining companies, Local authorities, Ministerial authorities (e.g., MOIT, EVN), and other stakeholders (e.g., international investors, NGOs). Include organizational charts or ownership structures if available."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Current challenges",
            "details": "Discuss the energy trilemma (security, affordability, sustainability), international market dependencies, environmental and social controversies, and any recent disruptions (e.g., fuel shortages, regulatory changes)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "Per-Plant Discussion",
        "description": "For each plant or plant complex, provide a narrative covering:",
        "subsections": [
          {
            "topic": "Development history and timeline",
            "details": "Include original plans (e.g., PDP versions), actual progress, and deviations. Use specific dates (e.g., MoU signing, groundbreaking, COD) and cite sources for each milestone."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Notable issues",
            "details": "Document delays, financing changes, ownership transfers, legal issues, controversies, technology changes, or environmental/social impacts. Cite primary sources (e.g., court rulings, company filings, NGO reports) and include direct quotes where relevant."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Current status confidence",
            "details": "Classify confidence as HIGH (verified by government decision, company annual report, or regulatory filing), MEDIUM (confirmed by multiple reputable news sources or secondary reports), or LOW (status uncertain, only found in older plans or unverified sources). Justify the confidence level in the Notes field."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "Structured Power Plants Table",
