            },
            {
              "name": "Access date",
              "description": "Date when the source was last accessed (YYYY-MM-DD)."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "section": "Statistical Summary Tables",
        "description": "Produce the following cross-tabulations from your inventory. Ensure all tables are internally consistent (e.g., row and column totals match).",
        "tables": [
          {
            "name": "Capacity by fuel × status",
            "description": "Total MWe in each cell (rows: Coal, Domestic gas, Imported LNG; columns: Operational, Under construction, Approved, Planned, Suspended, Cancelled, Retired). Include row and column totals. Reconcile with known national totals (e.g., PDP8)."
          },
          {
            "name": "Top provinces",
            "description": "The 15 provinces with the highest total thermal capacity (all statuses combined), showing breakdown by fuel (Coal, Gas, LNG). Include a map or geographic distribution analysis if possible."
          },
          {
            "name": "Timeline of additions",
            "description": "Capacity entering service by period: pre-2005, 2005–2010, 2011–2015, 2016–2020, 2021–2025, 2026–2030, post-2030. Break down by fuel type. Include a column for 'Retired capacity' if data is available."
          },
          {
            "name": "Data quality summary",
            "description": "Count of plants by confidence level (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW) and fuel type. Include a column for 'Sources not found' if applicable."
          }
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "For each table, include a brief narrative explaining key trends, anomalies, or uncertainties.",
          "Flag any discrepancies between your inventory and reference documents (e.g., PDP8, IEA reports). Explain potential reasons for differences (e.g., different inclusion criteria, status definitions).",
          "If a table cannot be completed due to missing data, note the gaps and suggest how they might be filled."
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "Data Quality and Reconciliation",
        "description": "Address the four quality dimensions explicitly:",
        "subsections": [
          {
            "topic": "Accuracy",
            "details": "List all known reference inventories (e.g., PDP8, IEA, Global Energy Monitor) and compare your results to them. Calculate precision, recall, and F1 score for plant identification and attribute accuracy if possible. Document any omissions or discrepancies."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Coherence",
            "details": "Verify internal consistency (e.g., no negative capacities, no duplicate units, row/column totals match). Reconcile contradictions between sources and document the rationale for your choices. Use the Notes field to flag unresolved inconsistencies."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Provenance",
            "details": "Ensure every data point in the inventory and summary tables traces back to at least one primary source. For high-impact claims (e.g., COD, capacity), provide two independent sources. Document any assumptions or interpolations."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Temporality",
            "details": "For each plant, specify the 'as-of' date for its status and attributes. For forward-looking claims (e.g., planned COD), note the source's publication date and any conditions (e.g., 'subject to financing'). Highlight status changes (e.g., from 'Planned' to 'Cancelled')."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "section": "Appendices",
        "description": "Include the following supplementary materials:",
        "subsections": [
          {
            "topic": "Glossary of terms",
            "details": "Define all technical terms, status categories, and abbreviations used in the inventory (e.g., 'COD', 'CCGT', 'PDP8')."
          },
          {
            "topic": "List of excluded plants",
            "details": "List any plants < 30MWe or non-thermal plants that were considered but excluded, with a brief rationale."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Data collection methodology",
            "details": "Describe your search strategy, inclusion criteria, and how you handled conflicting information. Include a list of keywords and sources searched."
          }
        ]
      }
